To Erik Rauch respond I thus:

First off, I'd like to say that I, and no doubt the others too, greatly
appreciate all the work you have been doing for Lojban in IRC and now the
FTP site.

I've dumped the code of my lojban semantic analyser in the FTP archive,
filename "analyser".

There is a fair amount of overlap between what might be potentially stashed
away on the FTP site, and what is already there in the list articles; I
leave to you the question of how this is to be resolved.

As soon as they are appropriately revised/updated, I will dump on the FTP
site my lujvo-making paper and my lujvo list.

A corpus of corrected and updated Lojban text is an important thing to have
around; once I get time, I'll start going through what text I've penned to
update it.

I've filled in some of the missing names in your 'stats' file, though
presumably it will need to be redone once you have the full list (I do
remember Art Protin, at the least, as having posted far more than 10
articles back in '91). It would make sense to list posters under name
rather than address, combining their totals. The stats certainly did yield
a few surprises, and I think the stats for the entire list corpus will
do so even more!


